A highly believable real-world photograph of a single Patchouli Knowledge (Touhou Project) fumo-style collectible plush doll, sitting on a light oak tabletop. Faithfully recognizable as a fumo plush, with an oversized broad rounded head, a tiny soft stuffed body, short stubby arms, and two little legs extending forward in the iconic seated pose. About 20 cm tall. It is a physical fabric toy, not a human, not an anime drawing, not a vinyl figure.

Patchouli's character details translated into sewn plush construction: lavender-purple fabric hair with blunt layered felt bangs and long broad fabric side locks; large purple embroidered anime eyes, a tiny simple stitched mouth and a calm slightly deadpan fumo expression. The face is smooth pale cream short-pile plush fabric, with flat embroidered features rather than glass eyes or modeled human anatomy. A soft pale lavender frilled mob cap carries a small yellow crescent moon made of felt and contrasting muted red and blue fabric bows. A simplified pale lavender long dress has subtly darker lavender vertical panels, a small gathered hem, and short stuffed arms. Preserve the chunky, endearing fumo proportions and simple sewn shapes rather than elaborate realistic human clothing. No book or extra accessories.

Photograph: three-quarter frontal view from approximately the plush's eye level, the entire doll including cap and feet comfortably inside a square frame, occupying about 70 percent of the image height. Soft daylight enters from a window to camera left. Realistic subtle shadows under the cap, at the arms and where the seated doll compresses against the table. Show fine short fabric pile, tiny loose fibers, restrained stitching, layered seams, slight stuffing asymmetry and believable cloth folds. The felt moon remains a matte fabric applique, not shiny metal. A natural 50mm-lens product-photo look, moderate depth of field: both eyes and most of the toy remain clearly focused while the distant neutral room background softly falls out of focus. Natural white balance, gentle contrast, tactile material detail, no dramatic cinematic grading, no glowing outlines, no CGI plastic sheen. No text, logos, watermark, packaging, hands, people or additional dolls.
